{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790254145,"nonce":"dbSTAE4XxvqEvE27BoGQ2kSAp9o=","title":"Nightly windows-x86_64 fails its smoke test: unregistered runtime symbols, CRLF breaks runtime metadata","message":"Every nightly since 2026-09-21 (first at 65cc59be) fails on windows-x86_64 only, in \"Smoke-test the binary it just built\":\n\n    error[IMPORT]: imported module `haxe.iterators.StringIteratorUnicode` failed to compile (1 error(s))\n        Non-constant runtime metadata argument in @access (0:0)\n    thread 'main' panicked at cranelift-jit-0.135.1/src/backend.rs:252:21:\n    can't resolve symbol haxe_dynamic_arith\n\nTwo independent causes.\n\n1. Runtime symbols. The Cranelift JIT on Windows resolves runtime symbols only from the plugin inventory (`register_symbol!` in runtime/src/plugin_impl.rs); macOS/Linux fall back to the process symbol table, so a missing entry is invisible there. Seven exports added during the 2026-09-20/21 conformance work were never registered: haxe_dynamic_truthy, haxe_dynamic_arith, haxe_dynamic_order, haxe_dynamic_to_slot, haxe_dynamic_to_f64, haxe_closure_register_entries, haxe_closure_dynamic_view. rayzor_mem_prefetch (runtime_mapping for rayzor.Mem.prefetch) was also missing.\n\n2. CRLF. Git for Windows checks out .hx files with CRLF. compilation/runtime_metadata.rs decided `@:meta` vs `@meta` by slicing the RAW source at the metadata span, but spans index the PREPROCESSED text, which `lines()` rewrites with `\\n`. With CRLF every line shifts by a byte, the slice no longer starts with `@:`, and `@:access(StringTools)` is treated as runtime metadata with a non-constant argument. Reproduced on macOS by converting StringIteratorUnicode.hx to CRLF. (Spans also diverge after any `#if` block for LF input; it happened to hold for the cases seen.)\n\nFix: register the symbols, plus a runtime unit test that every `#[no_mangle] extern \"C\"` export is in the inventory (allowlist for host-only exports); record `compile_time` on parser::Metadata from the token and use it instead of the span slice.","files":null}]}